 ## Background
-This method was introduced in the context of the Visualization Toolkit (VTK) to enhance realism and depth perception in volume visualizations, particularly in simulators where locating tools or objects is critical [S1]. It was implemented in `vtkGPUVolumeRayCastMapper2` to allow shadow receiving without the computational penalty of rendering the volume twice [S1]. The approach leverages existing shadow map infrastructure (`vtkShadowMapPass`, `vtkShadowMapBakerPass`) and extends it to volumetric ray casting by adding a receiver flag and shadow lookup during traversal [S1].
